                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A very niche game that oddly combines 1995-era 3D characters and video; some characters are FMV only, some will be CG and some will be both. I found the puzzles a bit easy, and the biggest challenge for me in the game was navigation of the small area.\n\nThe game is atmospheric and the sound design is pretty decent. My favorite puzzles had to do with combining info from books with actions in-game, forcing you to read the lore. There wasn't anything too challenging, though (nothing close to Riven's puzzle requiring you to know numbers in two different alien languages)\n\nIt was fun for a quick playthrough, and it reminded me of Sierra's Shivers. The area the game takes place in is about the size of a single Myst island, so it is perfect to play in a single afternoon during this spooky month.",
